  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Widening Learning Pathways for Lifelong Learning</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme contributes to Pacific SIDS widen learning pathways to promote education and training opportunities throughout lifecycles and to enhance relevant skills and knowledge to achieve individual and societal development and wellbeing. Building on to 40C5 and 41C5 work, this will be done through integrating greening/sustainable aspects in TVET curricula and provision, CONFINTEA VII Marrakech Framework of Action monitoring and Pacific community of practice support, country support towards ratification and implementation of Asia Pacific Regional and Global Conventions on Higher Education, national university development support as well as exploring regional or inter-regional university consortium. The workplan supports Pacific exchanges in promotion of STEM education with gender equity in collaboration with Science sector, IISTEM and partners including CROP agencies. It links with OP8.</narrative>
  </description>
